(rectangle (start 22.86 129.54) (end 275.59 213.36) (stroke (width 0) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "3a23465d-fe46-5b1a-a176-ef1d5b3ce8f2"))
(text "Leg L- (OPA1622, halves in parallel)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 24.13 128.27 0) (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3f3c40b8-7070-55bf-8468-af40b50d0cc3"))
(text_box "Notes\n1. Function: two OPA1622, one per leg of the right channel of the 4.4 mm output; each half its own\n   difference amplifier (R1 = R3 1.00 kΩ, R2 = R4 1.62 kΩ, gain 1.62, 100 pF across R2 and R4),\n   feedback at the half's pin, 1.0 Ω ballast to the leg (ADR 0012; BOM v1 lines 19, 37, 107, 108).\n2. Absent state: HPA_BAL_EN pulled down on the host side: shutdown. A disabled output is not\n   high-impedance: never fitted but unpowered while the other stage plays (feature blocks #33-34);\n   left off only with its jack, as one output module (blk.hp-out-se, -bal: feature blocks #51-52).\n3. R4 returns to ground; the jack's ground pin joins it at the jack.\n4. Thermal pad (EP) to V- (PCB-A-08). Halves of a package symmetric, legs symmetric (PCB-A-09, -10).\n5. Rails from blk.hpa-bal, after links H20 #9 and #10 (power tree §4.12).\n6. Unless noted: network resistors 0.1 % 0603 thin film, network capacitors C0G 50 V 0603;\n   ballast 1 % 0603; decoupling X7R 0402. Mute shunt footprints (BOM v1 line 100): open item." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 275.59 219.71 0) (size 129.54 29.21) (margins 1.905 1.905 1.905 1.905) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6e46b11b-0495-5246-9567-4b0b6ee358ac"))
